cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research framework, please cite the repository
  and the specific version consulted.
type: generic
title: 'Autonomous Questioning Structural Intelligence (AQSI): Question Discovery, Multi-Granularity Influence Scoring, Structural Relay, and Research Governance'
authors:
  - family-names: Tan
    given-names: Sizhe
repository-code: 'https://github.com/sizhet/Autonomous-Questioning-Structural-Intelligence'
url: 'https://github.com/sizhet/Autonomous-Questioning-Structural-Intelligence'
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A theory-first research framework for autonomous question discovery,
  multi-granularity directional influence scoring, historical question
  intelligence, question portfolios, exploration contracts, structural relay,
  cross-domain transfer, and strategic research governance. The repository
  proposes specifications, cases, extensions, and validation hypotheses;
  it does not claim experimentally verified autonomous scientific discovery
  or recursive self-improvement.
keywords:
  - autonomous questioning
  - structural intelligence
  - question discovery
  - multi-granularity influence
  - historical question intelligence
  - structural relay
  - research governance
  - cross-domain transfer
  - recursive improvement
